# Spec for Threat Modeling code labs

Same lab rules as `.sscr-parts/SPEC.prompt`. Read `.sscr-parts/01-authentication.md` for tone and snippet shape.

Shared system: a billing API called ledger. Browser, API, Postgres, a card processor, and a worker on a queue. Trust boundaries are browser to API, API to processor, queue to worker, and tenant to tenant.

Every lab is one threat a modeler would write down, then the handler that makes it true and the handler that closes it. Do not clone the Secure Source Code Review catalog. Stay on the assigned point.

No `{{`, no `{%`, no template braces. ASCII only. End the file with a line containing only `---`.
